{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", writes it, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","type":"reference"},{"text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pipelines API’s "},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with the key as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bearer token and "},{"code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,500 calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call or traits are sent. Its "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its "},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"goes in the spec’s "},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fields ("},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the request unless the call has one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even beside ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each endpoint counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its first send. Segment deduplicates calls by ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops most duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices (","type":"text"},{"code":"User Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"User Suppressed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Device Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan when the destination is made.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding","symbolKind":"module","title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Segment","title":"Sending to Segment"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack","title":"Sending to RudderStack"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines","title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines."}],"references":{"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes Segment’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecEncodingError":{"title":"SegmentSpecEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecencodingerror","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segment","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0A6RegionO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transport","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSetupError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/segment(writekey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Segment source of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"writeKey"},{"type":"text","text":", in a workspace in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]}},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"type":"topic","title":"batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Segment spec’s limits on one request, which Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accept: 2,500 calls, 500,000 bytes of body, and 31,999 bytes of one call."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/CustomerIORegion":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The region of a Customer.io workspace, which decides the Pipelines API endpoint its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"posted to."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"CustomerIORegion","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CustomerIORegion","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/customerioregion","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CustomerIORegion","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:cloc